column5:
pi parsePiMessagesEvent uses ONLY THE FIRST line starting with "data:" (.find) and ignores the rest; ri joins ALL data lines with "
" (SSE-spec behavior, shared SseJsonParser). Scenario A: event "data: {"a":1}
data: junk

" -> pi yields {"a":1}; ri parses "{"a":1}
junk" which fails JSON and the frame is silently dropped. Scenario B: event "data:
data: {"a":1}

" -> pi finds first data line "" (falsy) and drops the whole event; ri parses "
{"a":1}" successfully. Only matters if the pi-messages backend ever emits multiple data lines per event.
